ges":"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6146643810","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/72#issuecomment-6146643810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/72","id":6146643810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABbl5XYg","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-13T13:28:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T13:28:06Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** INDEPENDENT\n**Automated operational score:** 70/100 — MEDIUM — APPROVE_WITH_COMMENTS\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **HIGH · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · Unrestricted inbound RDP (port 3389) permitted from 0.0.0.0/0**\n  - Category rationale: The NSG security_rule 'AllowRDP' permits inbound TCP port 3389 from source_address_prefix '0.0.0.0/0' to any destination. This is a concrete, demonstrated configuration that exposes RDP to the public internet. The inline comment acknowledges the rule is 'deliberately unrestricted' and 'insecure'. The SEC-001 policy requires that no resource be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified; the code comment asserts testing justification but provides no scope-limiting control such as a restricted source prefix, JIT access policy, or time-bound mechanism. The priority-301 rule is evaluated before the priority-4096 DenyAllInbound rule, confirming it is effective.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_group.nsg, security_rule 'AllowRDP': direction='Inbound', access='Allow', protocol='Tcp', destination_port_range='3389', source_address_prefix='0.0.0.0/0', priority=301. Comment reads: '# TC03: Deliberately unrestricted RDP access. This insecure rule is for controlled security testing only.'\n  - Analysis: The NSG resource 'azurerm_network_security_group.nsg' contains a security_rule named 'AllowRDP' at priority 301 that allows inbound TCP traffic on port 3389 from any source address (0.0.0.0/0) to any destination in the subnet. RDP exposed to the public internet is a high-value attack surface: it is routinely targeted by brute-force, credential-stuffing, and exploitation campaigns. The in-code justification ('controlled security testing only') does not configure a technical restriction on who can reach the port.\n  - Impact: Any host on the public internet can attempt RDP connections to resources in subnet-demo (10.0.1.0/24). Even in a research or testing context, a reachable RDP port can be exploited to gain unauthorised interactive access, pivot to connected networks, or be used as a command-and-control foothold if credentials are weak or a vulnerability exists in the RDP implementation.\n  - Recommendation: Restrict source_address_prefix to a specific trusted IP range (e.g., the organisation's egress NAT IP or VPN gateway prefix) rather than 0.0.0.0/0. If unrestricted access is genuinely required for a time-limited test, document a planned removal date and consider using Azure Just-In-Time VM access or a Bastion host to avoid persistent public exposure. Remove or tighten the rule immediately after testing is complete.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6146643810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/s